<title>BELGIUM: UCB in 150 mln Bfr Chinese joint venture.</title>
<headline>UCB in 150 mln Bfr Chinese joint venture.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian pharmaceuticals and chemicals firm UCB said on Friday it had signed an agreement with Chinese group SBC to set up a joint venture in Shanghai for the production of choline chloride.</p>
<p>The investment in the joint venture - expected to have an annual turnover of about 500 million Belgian francs - would be 150 million francs, UCB said in a statement.</p>
<p>The plant would have capacity of 12,000 tonnes a year and employ 40 people.</p>
</text>
